<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Arranging identical colored balls in a row</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>(a)</b> In how many ways can \({@pa@}\) identical Red balls and \({@pb@}\) identical Blue balls be arranged in a row?</p>
<p>Number of ways = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p><b>(b)</b> In how many ways can \({@pc1@}\) identical Red balls, \({@pc2@}\) identical Blue balls, and \({@pc3@}\) identical Green balls be arranged in a row?</p>
<p>Number of ways = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution:</b></p>

<p>When arranging \(n\) items that contain identical groups of sizes \(r_1, r_2, \dots\), divide \(n!\) by the factorial of each group:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle P = \frac{n!}{r_1! \times r_2! \times \cdots}\)</p>

<p><b>Part (a): Arranging {@pa@} Red and {@pb@} Blue balls</b><br>
Total number of balls: \(n = {@pa@} + {@pb@} = {@pn@}\). Substitute into the formula, expand \({@pn@}!\) until it matches \({@big1@}!\), and cancel:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle P = \frac{{@pn@}!}{{@pa@}! \times {@pb@}!} = \frac{{@num1_factors@} \times {@big1@}!}{{@big1@}! \times ({@den1_small@})} = \frac{{@num1_val@}}{{@den1_val@}} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Number of ways} = {@ta1@} }\)</p>

<p><b>Part (b): Arranging {@pc1@} Red, {@pc2@} Blue, and {@pc3@} Green balls</b><br>
Total number of balls: \(n = {@pc1@} + {@pc2@} + {@pc3@} = {@pnc@}\). Substitute into the formula, expand \({@pnc@}!\) until it matches \({@g1@}!\), and cancel:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">\(\displaystyle P = \frac{{@pnc@}!}{{@pc1@}! \times {@pc2@}! \times {@pc3@}!} = \frac{{@num2_factors@} \times {@g1@}!}{{@g1@}! \times ({@den2_g2@}) \times ({@den2_g3@})} = \frac{{@num2_val@}}{{@den2_val@}} = {@ta2@}\)</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px; font-size: 1.2em;">\(\displaystyle \boxed{ \text{Number of ways} = {@ta2@} }\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
